<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Egnātĭus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Roman proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> L. Egn. Rufus, <i>friend of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 43 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 7, 18, 4 al.</span></i>—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> M. Egn. Rufus, <i>the name of an edile</i>, 733 A. U. C., <i>who set on foot a conspiracy against Augustus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
				91 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Clem. 1, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Brev. Vit. 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 1, 10</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Egnātĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Egnatius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scelus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					2, 93</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Egnatia</span></b> 
			Maximilla, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15, 71</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
